  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 43.5% acc, while config_043 (image_only, imagenet_vit_l) achieves only 22.7% acc, suggesting RNA contributes substantially. However, we have no RNA-only baseline, so we cannot determine whether the 21-point gain comes from additive modality contributions or synergy. Question: config_031 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) isolates the RNA contribution using the same encoder and profile setting as config_001. Together with the two completed experiments, this trio decomposes the multimodal benefit: if RNA alone is ~35-40%, the multimodal gain is modest; if it is ~20-25%, the combination is synergistic and further multimodal optimization is warranted. Why best next: this is a single-variable change (removing image) from the current best, it resolves a fundamental uncertainty about whether RNA is the primary signal carrier, and it directly informs whether subsequent budget should be spent optimizing fusion/aggregation in the multimodal setting or exploring RNA-only or alternative encoder configurations."
}

